<title>LEBANON: Bank of Lebanon weekly CDs raise 34 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Bank of Lebanon weekly CDs raise 34 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Lebanon issued certificates of deposit dated October 11 to commercial banks worth 34 billion Lebanese pounds compared with 11 billion last week.</p>
<p>The Bank sold 45-day CDs worth one billion pounds compared with three billion last week. It sold 60-day CDs worth 33 billion pounds compared with eight billion last week.</p>
<p>Interest rates on the 45- and 60-day CDs were 12.75 percent and 13.50 percent respectively, unchanged for the fifth week running.</p>
<p>($1 = 1,557.75 Lebanese pounds)</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (9611) 864148 645456 353078 602057</p>
